Accept an HTTPS-terminate and a TLS-passthrough listener on one port when the
passthrough hostname is strictly narrower than the HTTPS one.

Downstream only: Gateway API leaves cross-protocol listeners on one port to
the implementation (kubernetes-sigs/gateway-api#4271), and upstream Cilium
waits for that before changing the rule. Drop it once a shipped Cilium
release accepts the pair on its own.

